**************************************************************
Boom Buds Network Notes
**************************************************************
Boom Buds plays network games on your local network.

One computer runs the Boom Buds LAN server and every
player opens the game from its address.  The server
only introduces the computers to each other: the
game itself flows directly between the browsers, so
on a LAN there is no noticeable delay.

It is not advisable to rapidly press the <ESC> key 
during transition screens since you would leave the
game.

~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Network Game Rules
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
When you are a server, the maximum number of clients
that can attach to you is four.

The server chooses the level and the number of wins,
starts the matches and advances the score screens.
Each computer sets up its own players (keyboard
layouts and gamepads) on the control selection screen;
the players of the other computers show up as 'NET.'
Only the server can add computer players.

All the features of a single computer game are
available in network games: trampolines, the swap
disease, the random powerup, hits on the head...

Diseases:  All diseases can be destroyed during a
  network game, whatever the 'Diseases Can Be
  Destroyed' option says.

Gold Bud:  The Gold Bud (Roulette Wheel) option is
  not available in Network play.

Artificial Intelligence:  The Ctrl-A shortcut to select 
  all AI players in the Controller Setup Screen is not 
  supported in Network play.

Lost players:  If a computer leaves the game, its
  players stand still until the round ends, or play
  on as computer players when 'Lost net players revert
  to AIs' is set to Yes on the server.


~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Performance Hints
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
A wired network gives the smoothest games.  Wi-Fi works
well too; if a game stutters, move closer to the access
point.
